<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Makassar War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1666–1669</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Makassar War (1666–1669) was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> (VOC), allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-palakka">Arung Palakka</a> of Bone, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-gowa">Sultanate of Gowa</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-hasanuddin">Sultan Hasanuddin</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bongaya">Treaty of Bongaya</a> (1667) forced Gowa to cede territory and accept a VOC trade monopoly, and the fall of its fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somba-opu">Somba Opu</a> in 1669 ended Makassar's role as an independent trading power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/makassar-war.jpg" alt="Makassar War" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Romeyn de Hooge (engraver / etcher) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AMH-6157-NA_The_conquest_of_Macassar_by_Speelman_from_1666_to_1669.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
